{"title":"2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1183a12017e48198b3352789cc39b223b17945d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/f/f9fdba4c6de0201cbc7486d4c825c8199074ad54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 40 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 50 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 100 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 400 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 800$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"424\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can figure out what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is. This would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/7852006e2f0e43cfe9d62f71a56c04056182929d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\% \\times 200 = \\frac{1}{10} \\times 200 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"223\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Next, we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the missing number. Setting up an equation, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5329069eb163f7c95c4c6c01b2798df1ccaf660.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\% \\times x = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/b/6abc359e8deb9c9500203ddb17ab1c5586f70c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5} \\times x = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a3599fd371f4dd9d3300c0a1adf232608e9d1f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 20 \\times 5 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"184\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the values to be equal, the missing number must be half of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> for the values to be equal because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d266246356f2963d20cdb78e7a91f961b7fd3f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\% \\times 2 = 20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"17\" />, so halving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> would cancel out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e163633a9718e9fc13fbe29b05d3a4ade9130f99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\times 2$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>This shows that the missing number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3c361f8c7bcc95fc052c2bb6d8829ae0b18bec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{200}{2} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"131\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Prob